ar graph. NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest_last"},{"type":"text","text":", whose ties follow set order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead. O((n + m) log n)."}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/independentSet":{"kind":"symbol","title":"ColoringStrategy.independentSet","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/independentset","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Colour classes one at a time: class k is a maximal independent set of the vertices not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coloured, built by repeatedly taking the one with the fewest neighbours among those still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available (the least index on ties) and making it and its neighbours unavailable. NetworkX","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"independent_set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose ties follow set order instead. O(χ (n + m) log n) for χ classes.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"independentSet"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet"}}}